body:
@coderabbitai Addressed in afd09a86e6 by identifying the failed check run directly instead of persisting a SHA.

Every miner event comes from a check-run object (`checks_json` → `emit_event_json`), and Evidence already renders that run's `html_url`. For CodeFactor that URL ends with the check-run id, e.g. `https://github.com/marcusquinn/aidevops/runs/140009050558` is check run `id: 140009050558` (verified with `gh api repos/marcusquinn/aidevops/commits/841a3cb070.../check-runs?check_name=CodeFactor`). That id pins the exact run that failed, so a later push to the PR cannot change which annotations are read.

The guidance in both renderers now says: read annotations for the check-run id that ends the `/runs/<check-run-id>` Evidence link; only if Evidence has no run link, look the id up from the failing commit (`<failing-sha>`, explicitly "not a newer PR head"). The `ci-failure-patterns.conf` record serves per-PR CI feedback, where the failing-checks list names the commit that failed, so its step 1 points at that commit. Adding a separate SHA line would duplicate a weaker identifier for the same run, so no event schema change was made.

