body:
@coderabbitai Valid. Fixed in 62b7c9f392.

Workflow-sourced events store the Actions run `html_url` (`/actions/runs/<id>`) as `run_url`, and that path also contains `/runs/<id>`, so the previous wording could treat a workflow-run id as a check-run id and skip the commit fallback.

The shared `codefactor_fix_guidance` definition (used by both renderers) now:
- reads annotations directly only for a native check-run link (`https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/runs/<check-run-id>`, no `/actions/` segment);
- for an `/actions/runs/<run-id>` link, resolves the commit with `gh api "repos/<owner>/<repo>/actions/runs/<run-id>" --jq .head_sha` (verified live: run 45853224315 → `f8afcc32d8...`), then looks up the CodeFactor check-run id from that failing commit; the same commit lookup applies when Evidence has no run link.

Verification: `test-gh-failure-miner-codefactor-guidance.sh` 36/36, ShellCheck clean, pre-commit ratchets pass.

