@coderabbitai <!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM68fRnH -->
Both findings were valid and are fixed in `.agents/scripts/pre-commit-hook.sh` (`_count_repeated_literals` and `_show_repeated_literals`). `sed` now masks `\\` as `@B@` and `\"` as `@Q@`, working left to right. Escaped quotes are no longer treated as delimiters, but they stay part of the literal's identity. Parity is handled because `\\` is consumed first, so a quote after an even run still closes the string.

I added regression cases to `tests/test-string-literal-ratchet.sh`: the mixed escaped-quote input counts 0, and `"path\\"` repeated three times counts 1. All 13 tests pass and shellcheck is clean.

