Verified; the scope objection does not apply. The description permits a `TODO.md` handoff, with only newly added `todo/tasks` briefs as optional additional files; it does not prohibit status changes in `TODO.md`. “Not a completed TODO update” describes publication pending review/merge, not a restriction on task statuses (see `.agents/scripts/pulse-todo-publication.sh:112-118`). The PR diff changes only `TODO.md`.

The updates match GitHub state: `gh issue view` confirms #40508 is CLOSED/COMPLETED and #40538 is CLOSED/NOT_PLANNED; `gh pr view` confirms #40509 is MERGED. Thus `TODO.md:2543` and `TODO.md:2558` correctly record completed and declined tasks respectively. No changes needed; reverting would restore stale statuses. `git diff --check` passes.

